  "data": {
    "body": "(10 points) Let $A$ be an $m \\times n$ matrix. Let $R$ be the reduced row echelon form of $A$. Which of the following statements must be TRUE?\n\n\n\n(i) $\\operatorname{Nul}(A)=\\operatorname{Nul}(R)$.\n\n(ii) $\\operatorname{Col}(A)=\\operatorname{Col}(R)$.\n\n(iii) $\\operatorname{Rank}(A)=\\operatorname{Rank}(R)$.\n\n(iv) If $A$ has a pivot position in every column, then $A \\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is consistent for any $\\mathbf{b}$ in $\\mathbb{R}^{m}$.\n\n(v) If $A$ is a square matrix and $\\operatorname{det}(R)=0$, then $\\operatorname{det}(A)=0$.",
